  "details": "A full 8-bit Int can represent 256 states, but in many cases (especially when switching item displays), the demand is often less than 10 states, which is completely redundant.\n\nIn order to make more use of parameters, a 4-bit Int can be simulated by 4 Bool type values ​​to represent 16 states, but this requires several extremely complex state machines to simulate. This brings huge troubles to development.\n\nTherefore, I hope there can be a built-in Int4 (4-bit Int) type to solve this problem.",
